ng and older adults' mental health.\n\n### Coping Strategies:\n\n- **Networking**: Building and maintaining professional connections can open up opportunities that are not advertised.\n- **Skill Development**: Engaging in continuous learning and skill development can make candidates more attractive to employers.\n- **Seeking Support**: Utilizing resources such as career counseling, unemployment benefits, and mental health services can provide much-needed support.\n- **Flexibility**: Being open to different types of roles or industries can increase chances of finding employment.\n\nThe experiences of unemployed individuals are diverse, and addressing these challenges often requires a combination of personal initiative and support from community and governmental resources."}
