ite their differences, share common struggles like financial insecurity, the emotional toll of job searching, and the challenge of maintaining motivation and hope. These insights likely underscore the broader societal issue of unemployment and the need for targeted support and policies to help individuals across the age spectrum find meaningful employment."}
