ilities, leaving less time and energy for learning new technologies.\n\n4. **Fear of Obsolescence**: There might be an underlying fear of becoming obsolete or incapable in a rapidly changing digital world.\n\nTo help bridge this gap, strategies such as offering user-friendly technology, providing training programs, and encouraging a positive attitude toward learning can be beneficial. Additionally, fostering environments where knowledge sharing between generations is encouraged can assist in making technology more accessible and less daunting for those who find it challenging."}
