at intergenerational collaboration could be beneficial, allowing older individuals to share their life experiences and perspectives while learning from the tech-savvy younger generation. This exchange not only helps bridge the digital divide but also fosters mutual understanding and respect between generations.\n\nOverall, the interview highlighted the diverse experiences and challenges faced by different age groups in keeping up with technology. It underscored the importance of empathy, patience, and open communication in helping everyone navigate the digital age, regardless of their starting point."}
