ts of its utility based on their life stage and needs.\n\n4. **Role of Education and Support**:\n   - **Educational Programs**: Schools and community programs can play a crucial role in bridging the digital divide by offering training and resources.\n   - **Peer Support and Mentorship**: Younger individuals can often serve as informal tech mentors for older generations, facilitating knowledge transfer and mutual understanding.\n\n5. **Future Implications**:\n   - **Continual Learning**: As technology evolves, ongoing education and adaptability will be crucial for all age groups.\n   - **Inclusive Design**: Developing technology that is user-friendly and accessible to people of all ages can help mitigate some of the challenges associated with rapid technological change.\n\nThis interview scenario underscores the importance of understanding and addressing the diverse experiences and needs related to technology use across different age groups."}
