tive Flexibility**: Younger people often exhibit greater cognitive flexibility, which allows them to adapt to new information and environments more easily. This flexibility can facilitate the learning of new technologies.\n\n5. **Support Systems**: The high schooler may have access to peer support and resources that make learning new technology easier, whereas the middle-aged individual might lack such support networks.\n\nUnderstanding these dynamics can help in designing educational programs and support systems that encourage technology adoption across all age groups, ensuring that no one is left behind in our increasingly digital world."}
