hnology.\n\n3. **Perceived Complexity**: New technologies can seem overly complex, leading to frustration and disengagement.\n\n4. **Lack of Immediate Relevance**: If the technology doesn't seem immediately useful or necessary, older adults might not see the value in investing time and effort to learn it.\n\nTo address these challenges, it is important to provide supportive environments that encourage learning at a comfortable pace, offer clear instructions, and demonstrate the practical benefits of new technologies. Tailored training programs and user-friendly designs can also help bridge the gap, making technology more accessible and less intimidating for older adults."}
