ence and competence in using new technologies.\n\n2. **Encouragement of Curiosity**: Encouraging a mindset of curiosity and exploration can help both older adults and younger individuals to see technology as a tool for discovery and creativity, rather than a burden.\n\n3. **Peer Support and Mentorship**: Creating opportunities for intergenerational learning, where older adults and younger individuals can learn from each other\u2019s experiences and perspectives, can be mutually beneficial.\n\n4. **Balance and Mindfulness**: Teaching the importance of balancing technology use with other activities can help prevent feelings of exhaustion and burnout.\n\nBy understanding the diverse experiences and attitudes towards technology, we can better support individuals in navigating the digital world in ways that are meaningful and enjoyable for them."}
