asses tailored to older adults can help bridge the gap.\n   - **Intergenerational Learning:** Encouraging younger people to teach older adults about technology can foster understanding and connection between generations.\n   - **User-Friendly Design:** Developing technology with user-friendly interfaces can make it more accessible to people of all ages.\n\n5. **Social Implications:**\n   - **Isolation vs. Connection:** While technology can lead to social isolation for some older adults, it can also provide opportunities for connection and engagement through video calls, social media, and online communities.\n   - **Economic Opportunities:** Being tech-savvy can open up new economic opportunities, such as remote work or online businesses.\n\n6. **Psychological Impact:**\n   - **Stress and Anxiety:** The pressure to keep up with technology can cause stress and anxiety, particularly for those who feel left behind.\n   - **Empowerment:** Conversely, mastering new technologies can be empowering and boost confidence.\n\nThis interview likely highlights these themes, offering insights into how different generations perceive and interact with technology. Understanding these dynamics can help society create more inclusive and supportive environments for all age groups as technology continues to evolve."}
